# =========================
# Reference voices (voice cloning) — MUST come after the *.wav rules above
# =========================
# `voices/` holds the reference recordings a character is cloned from: source
# assets, not output. The blanket `*.wav` (twice, lines ~35 and ~105) swept them
# up, and since git does not track empty directories, nobody who cloned the repo
# saw `voices/` at all — the character voices simply were not there.
!voices/
!voices/*.wav
